{"id":"28cf05cbcc42beeb","subject":"go:golang.org/x/exp","time":"2025-06-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.0.0-20250620022241-b7579e27df2b"},"statement":"In golang.org/x/exp/trace, Value.Uint64() replaces Value.ToUint64() and panics unless the value is ValueUint64; Value.String() returns the raw string for ValueString, but a formatted representation for other kinds. Use v.Uint64() for a uint64 value or v.String() for a string value, according to v.Kind().","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/exp/+/b7579e27df2b8f70ede8041e7f4e69f0b099221f:trace/value.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:08:29.343562109Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"63d22044780c1758","subject":"go:golang.org/x/exp","time":"2025-07-18T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.0.0-20250718183923-645b1fa84792"},"statement":"The golang.org/x/exp/stats functions Mean, MeanAndStdDev, Median, and Quantiles accept and return user-defined float64 types through a type parameter constrained by `~float64`; for example, `type Celsius float64; mean := stats.Mean([]Celsius{1, 2})` returns a Celsius.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/exp/+/645b1fa84792ddcfd00e558a922fec54abd075e0:stats/stats.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:08:37.259026522Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"0cf77df220b51b91","subject":"go:golang.org/x/exp","time":"2025-11-25T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.0.0-20251125195548-87e1e737ad39"},"statement":"golang.org/x/exp/stats.Quantiles independently infers the floating-point type of values and quantiles, allowing different defined types whose underlying type is float64; for example, `stats.Quantiles([]Celsius{1, 2}, 0.5)` accepts untyped quantile constants and returns `[]Celsius`.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/exp/+/87e1e737ad395e640ddfb035b7b880dd28f73164:stats/stats.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:08:48.641274369Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"c49ecccffe61b0d6","subject":"go:golang.org/x/exp","time":"2025-12-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.0.0-20251219203646-944ab1f22d93"},"statement":"golang.org/x/exp/trace provides MakeStack, MakeEvent, EventConfig[T], StackSample, MakeGoStateTransition, MakeProcStateTransition, Uint64Value, and StringValue for constructing trace events and values; for example, `e, err := trace.MakeEvent(trace.EventConfig[trace.Metric]{Time: t, Kind: trace.EventMetric, Details: metric})` constructs an event from typed metric details.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/exp/+/944ab1f22d936eefb8f6260ecd2053101d8d7b2a:trace/event.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:08:56.153957135Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d03b8a67116f44f5","subject":"go:golang.org/x/exp","time":"2026-02-18T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.0.0-20260218203240-3dfff04db8fa"},"statement":"golang.org/x/exp requires Go 1.25.0 or newer; modules using it must declare or otherwise use a Go toolchain supporting the Go 1.25 language and module requirements.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/exp/+/2735e65f0518bac4f30f0042ea19b4b5b14dcbf7:go.mod","added":"2026-10-25T20:09:04.943282942Z","by":"agent"}
