{"id":"07b261941422d0c4","subject":"go:golang.org/x/exp","time":"2025-07-18T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.0.0-20250718183923-645b1fa84792"},"statement":"The new golang.org/x/exp/stats package provides descriptive statistics functions Mean, MeanAndStdDev, Median, and Quantiles; for example, `median := stats.Median([]float64{1, 2, 3})` computes the median, and these functions panic on empty input slices.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/exp/+/542afb5b7346d69c3c878cfdd23a583e8524294d:stats/stats.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:10:01.388346111Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"8b0f10a55d6cd66c","subject":"go:golang.org/x/exp","time":"2025-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.0.0-20250819193227-8b4c13bb791b"},"statement":"golang.org/x/exp/trace.FlightRecorder handles end-of-generation signals in the trace stream, passing them through without treating them as event batches or counting them toward the recorded generation size.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/exp/+/8b4c13bb791bae70eaa167bceb906b9d1c3082d2:trace/flightrecorder.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:10:07.023642752Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ba069eb841a43f3a","subject":"go:golang.org/x/exp","time":"2026-08-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.0.0-20260820122028-d6e0b57b1a69"},"statement":"In v0.0.0-20260820122028-d6e0b57b1a69, the typeparams aliases and wrappers that are explicitly marked deprecated direct users to their standard-library equivalents (for example, use `types.NewTypeParam` instead of `typeparams.NewTypeParam`), and `typeparams.Enabled` is deprecated because type parameters are always enabled. However, not every compatibility helper is marked deprecated: `ForTypeSpec` and `ForFuncType`, for example, have no deprecation notice.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/exp/+/50dc527dd6c74676d57de702ab3cb721e2e202de:typeparams/typeparams.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:10:13.519326444Z","by":"agent"}
